    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOFpg0Ns75aS8e",
      "title": "Add WAKU token to Base",
      "author": "antoine-wak",
      "number": 1345,
      "body": "**Description**\r\n\r\nAdd WAKU (Wakweli) to the token list for Ethereum and Base.\r\n\r\n- Ethereum: `0x93F014930d90A0D0f17B079f71D9aA5f3ADf2b27`\r\n- Base: `0x4d6B62861D1F60e864fD7C913f840d70b2713D0c`\r\n\r\nThe pair is already live on the native OP Standard Bridge: 5,960,018.25 WAKU qre\r\nheld on Base, matching the amount escrowed in the L1StandardBridge to the wei, and\r\nthe bridge's `deposits[l1][l2]` accounting agrees. This PR only adds the metadata so\r\nthe token is selectable in Superchain bridge front-ends.\r\n\r\nThe Base token is an `OptimismMintableERC20` on the standard L2 bridge\r\n(`0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000010`), with `l1Token()` and `remoteToken()`\r\nboth returning the Ethereum address above. Both contracts are verified.\r\n\r\n**Tests**\r\n\r\n`pnpm validate --datadir ./data --tokens WAKU` passes with no errors and no warnings.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\n`logo.svg` is 256x256 and pure vector: one `<circle>` and one `<path>`, with no\r\nembedded raster image, no text elements and no external references.\r\n\r\n**Metadata**\r\n\r\nN/A",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/ethereum-optimism.github.io",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-01T15:37:50Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 22,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOFpg0Ns75eU73",
      "title": "Add wRATR (Wrapped Ratatoskr) on Base",
      "author": "NexusAther",
      "number": 1346,
      "body": "Adds **Wrapped Ratatoskr (wRATR)** — a Base ERC-20 at `0xDeb6265cEE49CC277A938452DEDAb2B8774210d1` (source-verified on BaseScan).\n\nwRATR is minted 1:1 against native RATR held in a public reserve via the Ratatoskr↔Base bridge. It is a custodial wrapper and is **not** deployed via the OP StandardTokenFactory / standard bridge, so `nobridge: true` is set (it is not intended for the Optimism Bridge app).\n\n- `name` / `symbol` / `decimals` match on-chain (`Wrapped Ratatoskr` / `wRATR` / `8`)\n- Base-only entry (no L1 token)\n- Standard ERC-20 — no fee-on-transfer or rebasing\n\nWebsite: https://ratatoskr.enchantedforestdefi.com\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/ethereum-optimism.github.io",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-01T21:03:47Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 15,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOFpg0Ns78B6EM",
      "title": "Add AAH (AliensAreHere) token on Base",
      "author": "justintx19-bit",
      "number": 1347,
      "body": "**Description**\n\nAdds `AAH` (AliensAreHere), an ERC-20 token deployed natively on Base.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Name | AliensAreHere |\n| Symbol | AAH |\n| Decimals | 18 |\n| Chain | Base (8453) |\n| Address | [`0x1E3a76e1C2768395Ed9C0d81f7Eb4b89dfE70B31`](https://basescan.org/token/0x1E3a76e1C2768395Ed9C0d81f7Eb4b89dfE70B31) |\n| Website | https://aliensarehere.com |\n\n**Why `nobridge: true`**\n\nAAH was deployed directly on Base and has no L1 counterpart, so it is not a\nbridged token and does not implement `l2Bridge()` / `l1Token()`. The standard\nbridge validation is therefore not applicable and `nobridge` is set to skip it.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Contract source is verified on Basescan.\n- `name`, `symbol` and `decimals` match on-chain values exactly.\n- One token, two files (`data/AAH/data.json` + `data/AAH/logo.svg`), no other changes.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/ethereum-optimism.github.io",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-07T12:19:51Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 15,
      "deletions": 0
    }
